      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "No, taking even a low dose of ibuprofen without a doctor's specific approval is dangerous because the interaction risk isn't a matter of \"tiny bit\" vs. \"big bit.\" It is safer to try an over-the-counter medication like acetaminophen (Tylenol) instead, as it doesn't affect your blood thinning. Please call your doctor's nurse line now; most offices answer immediately for these urgent medication questions outside of office hours. Do take the recommended Tylenol alternative while you wait for their advice.",
